SUMMARY:Open Book\, Open Mind; Michael Luo\,v”Strangers in the Land"
DESCRIPTION:Open Book\, Open Mind; Michael Luo\, “Strangers in the Land: Exclusion\, Belonging\, and the Epic Story of the Chinese in America.”\nJoin Montclair Public Library for another great author conversation! Co-presented by AAPI New Jersey. Register now at https://tinyurl.com/OBOMStrangers\nThe executive editor of The New Yorker discusses his landmark study of the Chinese in America with Matthew Purdy\, editor at large of The New York Times.. “You can’t paint a complete picture of America without [the story of Chinese Americans]\, and the New Yorker journalist Michael Luo tells it persuasively in ‘Strangers in the Land‘… [The book] succeeds through its little biographies of individuals – a range of quirky and fascinating figures\, both Chinese and white\, who drive the narrative. . . [and offer] a view on the full complexity of American immigration.” ―The New York Times Book Review\nDoors open at 6 p.m. The discussion will be followed by an audience Q&A and book sales and signing with Watchung Booksellers. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/open-book-open-mind-michael-luovstrangers-in-the-land/
